name: "__NAME__"
version: "__VERSION__"
origin: "dns/karidns"
comment: "High-performance authoritative DNS server for FreeBSD with Capsicum sandboxing"
arch: "__ARCH__"
www: "https://github.com/NoelMinamino/KariDNS"
maintainer: "noel@karidns.org"
prefix: "/usr/local"
licenselogic: "single"
licenses: [
    "MIT"
]
desc: <<EOD
KariDNS is a FreeBSD-native authoritative DNS server engineered for ultra-low latency,
high throughput, and strict security via Capsicum sandboxing and lock-free RCU architecture.
Includes the dag protocol client/fuzzer, karictl management utility, karicheck syntax validator, and karidns-tapstat dnstap query statistics.
__DB_DESC__
EOD
categories: [
    "dns",
    "net",
    "sysutils"
]
conflicts: [ __CONFLICTS__ ]
provides: [ __PROVIDES__ ]
scripts: {
    pre-install: <<EOD
pw groupshow karidns >/dev/null 2>&1 || pw groupadd karidns
pw usershow karidns >/dev/null 2>&1 || pw useradd karidns -g karidns -h - -d /nonexistent -s /usr/sbin/nologin -c "KariDNS server"
EOD
    post-install: <<EOD
install -d -o root -g wheel -m 0755 /var/run/karidns
EOD
}
messages: [
    {
        type: "install",
        message: <<EOD
karidns runs as the user karidns, which this package created: copy /usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf.sample to
/usr/local/etc/karidns/karidns.conf (its user and group are karidns) and edit it. A configuration of an earlier version that names the
user bind or named keeps running as that user. An existing /var/log/named is left as it is; when it is missing, the rc script creates
it for the user and group of the configuration (or karidns_log_owner of rc.conf) and refuses to start when it cannot tell them
(docs/distribution.md "The user karidns"). karidns-signer and karidns-webadmin 0.7 require karidns-zone and karicheck, which the
server packages provide since 0.7: with pkg add, upgrade this package before them (docs/distribution.md 2.6).
EOD
    },
    {
        type: "remove",
        message: <<EOD
The user and group karidns, /var/run/karidns and /var/log/named (made by the rc script) are left in place (a configuration and the logs may still use them).
To remove them when nothing else uses them: pw userdel karidns (it removes the group karidns too), rm -r /var/run/karidns /var/log/named.
EOD
    }
]
deps: {
__DEPS__
}
files: {
__FILES__
}
